.TH LIBUSB_HANDLE_EVENTS 3 "March 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
libusb_handle_events, libusb_handle_events_timeout, libusb_handle_events_completed, libusb_get_pollfds \- drive libusb event processing
.SH LIBRARY
.B libusb
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <libusb.h>
.PP
.BI "int libusb_handle_events(libusb_context *" ctx ");"
.PP
.BI "int libusb_handle_events_timeout(libusb_context *" ctx ", struct timeval *" tv ");"
.PP
.BI "int libusb_handle_events_completed(libusb_context *" ctx ", int *" completed ");"
.PP
.BI "const struct libusb_pollfd **libusb_get_pollfds(libusb_context *" ctx ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions run the libusb event loop.
The loop reaps completed asynchronous URBs, services the event-interrupt pipe,
and processes USB hotplug changes detected through the backend event source.
.PP
.BR libusb_handle_events ()
waits using the library default timeout.
.BR libusb_handle_events_timeout ()
uses the caller-provided timeout.
.BR libusb_handle_events_completed ()
returns immediately if
.I *completed
is already non-zero.
.PP
.BR libusb_get_pollfds ()
returns a NULL-terminated array of poll descriptors that can be integrated into
an external event loop.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The event-handling functions return 0 on success or a negative
.B LIBUSB_ERROR_*
code on failure.
.BR libusb_get_pollfds ()
returns a dynamically allocated pollfd list or NULL on allocation failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B LIBUSB_ERROR_OTHER
No usable libusb context could be resolved.
.TP
.B LIBUSB_ERROR_NO_MEM
Internal hotplug or pollfd bookkeeping allocation failed.
.TP
.B LIBUSB_ERROR_IO
A backend event or URB reap operation failed.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
while (!done) {
    if (libusb_handle_events_timeout(ctx, &(struct timeval){1, 0}) != 0)
        break;
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libusb_init (3),
.BR libusb_submit_transfer (3),
.BR libusb_hotplug_register_callback (3)
